language sdl-mvp1-exercise version 0.1.

feature LiveMachineInspection.
feature InspectBuckingAlternatives.
feature ManageAptDefinitions.
feature ChangeUiPresentation.
feature InspectConnectionHealth.
feature RecoverUncertainAction.
feature OperateSimulation.
feature OperateMachineInputs.
feature InspectRecordedEvidence.
feature RequestSoftwareStop.
feature InspectMachineWithoutBucking.
feature RecordProduction.
feature InspectUiDiagnostics.
feature StopRuntimeCleanly.

LiveMachineInspection describes "Inspect fresh machine/sensor/state evidence without taking domain authority.".
InspectBuckingAlternatives describes "Inspect current valid one-best and background alternatives with explicit pending/stale state.".
ManageAptDefinitions describes "Import, inspect, edit, store/export and explicitly activate supported APT definitions.".
ChangeUiPresentation describes "Change presentation and share values while retaining live semantic context.".
InspectConnectionHealth describes "Recover coherent state and explain source/session/delivery currentness.".
RecoverUncertainAction describes "Recover a submitted action's result without accidental duplicate execution.".
OperateSimulation describes "Control/inspect deterministic simulated target through its separate control plane.".
OperateMachineInputs describes "Use permitted normalized operator input through public command contracts.".
InspectRecordedEvidence describes "Inspect/export/replay bounded diagnostic evidence into explicit isolated targets.".
RequestSoftwareStop describes "Request an identified software stop while retaining diagnostics and explicit safety scope.".
InspectMachineWithoutBucking describes "Continue Machine observation and permitted input when Bucking is unavailable.".
RecordProduction describes "Retain authoritative cut facts with economic/measurement/calibration lineage.".
InspectUiDiagnostics describes "Explain unhandled routing, handler failures and bounded diagnostic loss.".
StopRuntimeCleanly describes "Stop owned work/connections and account for pending durable state.".
